            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Louis Braille</strong><br>\nLouis Braille was born in 1809 in Coupvray, France, and at the age of three, he had an accident that resulted in blindness. Despite his disability, he excelled in his education at a school for blind children in Paris, which was one of the first of its kind. His early life was marked by a quest for knowledge and a desire to be treated equally despite his visual impairment.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Invention of Braille</strong><br>\nWhile at the school for the blind, Louis was introduced to a system of reading using raised dots, invented by Charles Barbier for military use. Louis Braille recognized the system's potential and by the time he was 15, he had refined Barbier's method into Braille, which was easier to use and more practical for the blind.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Braille System</strong><br>\nThe Braille system Louis invented is based on patterns of raised dots that represent letters, numbers, and punctuation marks. This system allows blind people to read and write independently. Braille's system was groundbreaking because it was universally designed to be used by people speaking any language.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
